  "description": "A self-contained OAuth 2.1 and OpenID Connect provider for ASP.NET Core. Two lines in Program.cs give you authorization code + PKCE, refresh tokens, client credentials, the device grant, PAR, introspection, revocation, dynamic client registration, RP-initiated logout and a discovery document any standard OIDC library can configure itself from. Multi-tenant, runs on SQLite, MySQL, PostgreSQL or SQL Server, and ships its own sign-in, consent and admin UI. Pair it with Ark.oAuth.Client for the application side.",
